      "name": "diagnosis",
      "output": "Revenue fell 6.24% over the 46-hour window from 2026-07-09 00:00:00 to 2026-07-10 21:00:00. The movement is concentrated in eCPM, which came in at 2.168 against a baseline of 2.4632, a 11.99% decline accounting for 198% of the movement. Requests actually rose 8.54% (572,415 vs 527,357.5), offsetting part of the loss at -127% of the movement; fill rate slipped 1.86% (0.7617 vs 0.7762) and render rate was flat at 0.9798.\n\nThis is localized, not broad. Video ad format moved -35.0% against -12.4% globally, carrying 100% of the unexplained movement and 57% of the whole incident. Secondary concentrations appear in Android 12 (-20.2% vs -12.0% globally, 73% of unexplained movement, 16% of the incident) and iPhone 14 (-24.8% vs -12.0%, 68% of unexplained, 14% of the incident). The shape is a clean switch: video eCPM went from 6.055 to 4.2 within a single hour at 2026-07-09 00:00:00, a change of -1.855 with 100% of the movement landing in that one hour, exactly on a day boundary. It reversed just as sharply at 2026-07-10 23:00:00 (4.127 to 4.298) after 46 hours. Interpretation: a step on a day boundary that reverses after a defined interval is consistent with something that schedules in days \u2014 a campaign flight, a config push, a nightly job \u2014 rather than an organic degradation or a fix.\n\nChecked and cleared: publisher_tier was uniform, all 3 values within 0.9% of the global -12.0%, largest outlier only 1.9% of the incident; category uniform across all 7 values within 1.8% of the global -12.4%, largest outlier 0.9%; vertical uniform across 8 values, largest outlier 0.5%; campaign_type uniform across 4 values, largest outlier 0.3%. Region and country were inconclusive \u2014 NAM and US lead their dimensions but each carries 0% of the unexplained movement, below the 50% concentration bar, so the movement is spread rather than concentrated. Fill rate and render rate held steady throughout, so this is not a delivery or rendering failure. Next step: pull video-format demand-side changes effective 2026-07-09 00:00:00 and ending 2026-07-10 23:00:00 \u2014 campaign flight dates, floor-price or config pushes, and any bidder participation change on video \u2014 and check why Android 12 and iPhone 14 absorbed disproportionate share.",
